[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119771,
      "id": "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff",
      "title": "Describing a Triangular Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the most specific listed description: identity before diagonal, and diagonal before upper or lower triangular. Choose Other only if none of these descriptions applies.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{13}=8\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/id": "34935959-d176-512d-b23c-05fbdacaa94b",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/id": "388e5655-6581-5ab9-82e4-d5b18ccabff6",
