    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the most specific listed description: identity before diagonal, and diagonal before upper or lower triangular. Choose Other only if none of these descriptions applies.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=6\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/id": "58d5658d-0b46-5b41-954d-dcf058fe272c",
