    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n\n$$\nC = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the most specific listed description: identity before diagonal, and diagonal before upper or lower triangular. Choose Other only if none of these descriptions applies.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${c}_{21}=2\\ne 0.$",
      ":question/id": "9436810a-9033-59e8-807d-42c7b99d8fc1",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
